WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.460
[intro music]

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.820
Good morning, Hank!
Good morning, Hank!

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:15.820
John: Perfect! You were supposed
to say "it's Tuesday," though.

00:00:15.820 --> 00:00:16.480
[crowd laughs]

00:00:16.480 --> 00:00:20.900
John: So, let's try it again, but this time
say "it's Tuesday." Ready? One, two three:

00:00:20.900 --> 00:00:22.600
Crowd: It's Tuesday!

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:24.120
I'm in the airport in New York City.

00:00:24.120 --> 00:00:26.460
Hank, I'm at the airport in Washington, D.C.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:32.000
So, for some reason that I don't understand, Penguin got me the couple's Valentine's special here at my

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:33.840
hotel in Washington, D.C.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:39.500
So last night I was treated to a dinner where I got two entrées, two appetizers, and two desserts.

00:00:40.360 --> 00:00:42.040
Sorry, Weight Watchers.

00:00:42.080 --> 00:00:44.100
And now I'm in the airport in Chicago.

00:00:44.100 --> 00:00:49.100
I know what you're wondering, Hank. You're wondering, "John, how are you getting from airport to airport?

00:00:49.860 --> 00:00:51.000
Are you using a hovercraft?

00:00:51.460 --> 00:00:52.860
Are you using Movie Magic?"

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:56.020
No, I'm using airplanes.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:01.320
And that's unfortunate, because you know what? Airplanes hate snow.

00:01:03.380 --> 00:01:11.220
Most of the people here at the moment are cameramen asking people what it's like that all the flights are being cancelled.

00:01:12.220 --> 00:01:14.200
So I thought I would recreate one of those interviews.

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:16.060
So, how do you feel about all these delays?

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:18.020
Um.... they suck.

00:01:18.020 --> 00:01:21.880
Could you actually, could you-could you-put my question back into your answer?

00:01:21.880 --> 00:01:26.460
Um... all these delays... of my flight... suck.

00:01:26.460 --> 00:01:32.000
Hank, I've spent 12 of the last 40 hours inside of airports, and you may be wondering how I pass the time when I'm here.

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.180
And the answer is simple: I've been hard at work on my 2007 celebrity death pool lineup.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:41.020
A celebrity death pool is where you pick 24 people who you think will die in the next year.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:46.660
It's really, you know, it's like... it's like good, clean fun. It's a way that I can give back.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:47.620
You know?

00:01:47.620 --> 00:01:53.860
The key to playing the game and still being able to live with yourself is to pick people that you're kind of rooting for.

00:01:54.140 --> 00:01:56.320
Or at least that you're OK with the idea.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:02:01.580
I mean, obviously you never want anyone to die, but if people have to, and, from what I understand, they do,

00:02:01.940 --> 00:02:03.800
they might as well be members of al-Qa'ida.

00:02:04.100 --> 00:02:11.960
So I'd like to say a preemptive goodbye to all those I hope we will be missing come January 1st, 2008.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:18.600
[song plays] This song is for the rats who hurled themselves into the ocean

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:25.880
[song cont's] when they saw that the explosives in the cargo hold were just about to blow

00:02:25.880 --> 00:02:32.360
[song cont's] This song is for the soil that's toxic clear down to the bedrock

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:38.340
[song cont's] where no thing of consequence can grow, drop your seeds there, let them go

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:44.840
[song cont's] let them all go!

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.120
Hank, I'll see you tomorrow.

